{
  "requirement": "The `PlainText` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct PlainText;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for PlainText;\nimpl Debug for PlainText;\nimpl Default for PlainText;\nimpl OutlineLang for PlainText;\nimpl Copy for PlainText;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText`**\n\nThe requirement is mostly an umbrella. It says `PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` with the extension, selection and fingerprint rules of the chapter. It also lists `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy` as trait implementations.\n\nThe detailed behaviour sits in three sibling requirements, and each has its own tests and reviews:\n- `plain-text.language` covers the extension claim and the fallback selection.\n- `plain-text.items` covers the line items and selectors.\n- `plain-text.fingerprints` covers the hash rules.\n\nJudged against its own text, the subject needs these checks:\n- `PlainText` exists as a public unit struct.\n- It implements `OutlineLang`.\n- It claims no extensions.\n- Its fingerprint scheme is the plain-text one.\n- Its trait implementations exist.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- Extensions and name: `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` asserts `plain.name() == \"plain-text\"` and `plain.extensions().is_empty()` on `languages::PlainText`. This checks the `OutlineLang` implementation and the claim of no extensions.\n- Fingerprint rules and scheme: `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries]` asserts these through `OutlineContent::from_source(\"note.txt\", ...)`, which falls back to plain text:\n  - the exact SHA-256 value for `hello`;\n  - whitespace-insensitivity;\n  - word-boundary sensitivity;\n  - the scheme `plain-text-structural-v1`.\n- Public struct and trait inventory: `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` compares the specified exports with generated rustdoc output.\n- Selection: the `OutlineContent::from_source` fallback is exercised by `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors`. That test is marked for `plain-text.items` and `plain-text.fingerprints`, so the selection and fallback obligations are covered by the refining requirements' own tests. They need no separate test here.\n\n**Trait implementations**\n\nIn `src/outline/languages/mod.rs`, `PlainText` comes from the `language!` macro with `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)]`. The derives are unconditional and do no transformation of their own. The generic `check` helper does not run on `PlainText`, but a derived `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug` or `Default` has no behaviour to test. The `OutlineLang` methods for `PlainText` are shared with the other bundled languages, which the same test does exercise. `PlainText` structural search is also tested, in `outline_only_languages_report_unsupported_structural_search`.\n\nI found no plausible violation of the subject's text that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "b45b2f19548ec7eabd67ea19330e68f013eaca7665581bec977b68c3838784b6",
